{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/926730-pentex-and-munitions","id":926730,"title":"Pentex and Munitions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-05T17:31:33-07:00","id":926730,"title":"Pentex and Munitions","content":"I have an arc cooked up for my game, where I want to have a rorqual beaching itself and being tormented due to sonar coming from a specific model of Pentex made submarines. Now my question is....which branch of Pentex would be useful for this or should I cook one up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T17:43:44-07:00","id":926739,"title":"","content":"because all &quot;evil&quot; things in werewolf must be thrown at the feet of one certain multinational holding company.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T17:55:25-07:00","id":926743,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I'd go with Endron or Full Force Solutions. Either one seems likely to have that sort of military contract.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T18:38:06-07:00","id":926758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/926730-pentex-and-munitions?p=926739#post926739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">because all &quot;evil&quot; things in werewolf must be thrown at the feet of one certain multinational holding company.....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My apologies that I decided to deal with the traditional corporate enemy, what was I thinking.<br /> <br /> Side note: In my own game I've hardly used Pentex because on average they aren't antagonists I tend to have an easy time cooking up plots for. Guess I'm just a failure to want to use Pentex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T22:10:33-07:00","id":926853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/926730-pentex-and-munitions?p=926743#post926743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I'd go with Endron or Full Force Solutions. Either one seems likely to have that sort of military contract.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I lean to Endron myself, they are the ones who seem like they would have subs in their arsenal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T22:53:08-07:00","id":926865,"title":"","content":"I'd go with Nastrum -- they're Pentex's default defense contractor.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, you could just make General Dynamics Electric Boat Division a Pentex subsidiary that nobody had made the connection to previously. Or Thyssen-Krupp, which did work for the Nazis once upon a time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T02:38:15-07:00","id":926941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/926730-pentex-and-munitions#post926730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an arc cooked up for my game, where I want to have a rorqual beaching itself and being tormented due to sonar coming from a specific model of Pentex made submarines. Now my question is....which branch of Pentex would be useful for this or should I cook one up?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could add GENES and Deepwater offshoots to the mix. They'd make for brilliant opponents, and no one can ever say no to cool underwater bases!<br /> (I'd skip the Technocracy conotations, though)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T07:57:27-07:00","id":927060,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone, I'll definately look into GENES, Deepwater and Nastrum. I have a copy of Blood Dimmed Tides floating around somewhere in my house. I've been wanting to use a Kami since I got the W20 Umbra book (for some reason they didn't click with me before that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T15:57:24-07:00","id":927320,"title":"","content":"Like others have said, I'd go with GENES and Nastrum. You could cook up some nasty stuff using them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T23:27:51-07:00","id":927465,"title":"","content":"I'd suggest not having the sub itself be Pentex built. It's far more terrifying if the sonar is the Pentex-built component, because it might wind up in military submarines throughout the world's navies. The potential for the mass extinction of the Rorqual should light a fire under any group's ass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T07:50:07-07:00","id":927615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/926730-pentex-and-munitions?p=927465#post927465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd suggest not having the sub itself be Pentex built. It's far more terrifying if the sonar is the Pentex-built component, because it might wind up in military submarines throughout the world's navies. The potential for the mass extinction of the Rorqual should light a fire under any group's ass.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a great point, I was trying to cook up some similar situation where the spread of this tech is a real threat. I figured the US military wouldn't be ok with their dealers building for all sorts of nations, but I didn't think about separating the sonar tech from the sub itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T00:06:16-07:00","id":927991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/926730-pentex-and-munitions?p=927615#post927615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I figured the US military wouldn't be ok with their dealers building for all sorts of nations...</div> </div> </div> </div>Lockheed Martin has the green-light to sell F-16Cs to Pakistan, F-16Ds to Iraq, and F-16Es to the UAE. Not to mention once upon a time Grumman's entire first production run of F-14A Tomcats didn't go to the U.S. Navy -- they went to Iran. Plus four anti-aircraft modified Spruance Class destroyers (which eventually became the Kidd Class) almost went to Iran too.<br /> <br /> So, I wouldn't be quite so sure about that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T07:53:35-07:00","id":928128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/926730-pentex-and-munitions?p=927991#post927991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lockheed Martin has the green-light to sell F-16Cs to Pakistan, F-16Ds to Iraq, and F-16Es to the UAE. Not to mention once upon a time Grumman's entire first production run of F-14A Tomcats didn't go to the U.S. Navy -- they went to Iran. Plus four anti-aircraft modified Spruance Class destroyers (which eventually became the Kidd Class) almost went to Iran too.<br /> <br /> So, I wouldn't be quite so sure about that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting, I wasn't sure how that worked. I have a player from a military family, and I'm a little nervous about getting something wrong and getting called out on it when its something important to the plot (like it going to not just the US military and becoming an internationally used contraption).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T10:36:04-07:00","id":928247,"title":"","content":"The selling of the sonar to foreign powers doesn't necessarily have to be green-lit by the US, Pentex could be selling them on the black market simply to spread the technology across the globe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4003-kristviljan","name":"Kristviljan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4003_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T10:55:57-07:00","id":928267,"title":"","content":"It depends on if it is considered to be dual use technology. If it is, then the US government has to approve international sales, though it pretty much rubber stamps most stuff for our allies (Iran got the military equipment from the US under the Shah, when it was our ally against the USSR). Military grade sonar is a big deal because it can be used for detecting our submarines, and I do not think that anyone except our closest allies, like Japan, are allowed to purchase any military grade sonar from US contractors. One potential twist would be the US military investigating why their new sonar is showing up on the black market, not knowing the real reason it exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T11:35:02-07:00","id":928302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/926730-pentex-and-munitions?p=928267#post928267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...the US government has to approve international sales, though it pretty much rubber stamps most stuff for our allies (Iran got the military equipment from the US under the Shah, when it was our ally against the USSR).</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite right. My point being however, that so long as the foreign power is aligned against the right countries, a certain &quot;the enemy of my enemy is my friend&quot; mindset tends to rule. For roughly 20 years Israel was quietly selling the Iranians parts for their fleet of American-built F-4s <i>after</i> the Shah's fall, and the U.S. sort of turned a blind eye. And I'm personally not real keen on selling <i>anything</i> to the Saudis or the Pakistanis.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/926730-pentex-and-munitions?p=928267#post928267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...One potential twist would be the US military investigating why their new sonar is showing up on the black market...</div> </div> </div> </div>Or NCIS agents disappearing without a trace for investigating it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 07-08-2016, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T14:37:51-07:00","id":928437,"title":"","content":"Which would cause its own investigation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Trust me, the military does not take it well when their investigators go missing, you hear about these type of things when you are in the service, and even the executives at Pentex would have to start sweating when a few admirals start asking questions. Of course, if admirals start disappearing, it starts becoming something that the general public takes seriously <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T22:44:41-07:00","id":928599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/926730-pentex-and-munitions?p=928437#post928437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trust me, the military does not take it well when their investigators go missing...</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither does the FBI. In the World of Darkness however, FBI Special Affairs agents go missing with disturbing frequency -- and you're never <i>really</i> sure if they got eaten by a vampire, got eaten by a werewolf, or got eaten by *(Miscellaneous).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T22:47:55-07:00","id":928603,"title":"","content":"Well toss in for me I'm planning on dealing with the Navy, I could sprinkle in some Chulorviah to avoid messy missing persons. They could just be well &quot;convinced&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T06:38:15-07:00","id":928715,"title":"","content":"True, though the Chulorvich are good all around bad guys unrelated the any particular faction, especially when you consider that eighty percent of humanity lives within an hour's drive of the sea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T11:17:35-07:00","id":935151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/926730-pentex-and-munitions?p=928599#post928599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neither does the FBI. In the World of Darkness however, FBI Special Affairs agents go missing with disturbing frequency -- and you're never <i>really</i> sure if they got eaten by a vampire, got eaten by a werewolf, or got eaten by *(Miscellaneous).</div> </div> </div> </div>Or got turned by a Vampire, awoke as a mage, found out they were Garou kinfolk,<br /> <br /> Got Enchanted by Unseelie Sidhe and kept as slaves...<br /> <br /> So many interesting fates, each better then the last.<br /> <br /> The mention of SAD here makes me think<br /> <br /> the Gift Geas seems pretty hard to defy.<br /> <br /> So if a elder philodex uses it on a SAD Agent hes assured of keeping his spy. from being able to blab everything , though he could yes be caught.<br /> <br /> Though I wonder what kind of consideration they'd be able to give to mystical compulsion in a investigation and punishment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 07-21-2016, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T12:57:22-07:00","id":935213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/926730-pentex-and-munitions?p=935151#post935151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The mention of SAD here makes me think<br /> <br /> the Gift Geas seems pretty hard to defy...<br /> <br /> ...Though I wonder what kind of consideration they'd be able to give to mystical compulsion in a investigation and punishment.</div> </div> </div> </div>To the latter point, it would (I think) depend on a series of considerations:<br /> <br /> 1. How receptive to the<i> idea </i>of paranormal powers is the agency (or its oversight body)? Even Twilight agencies have bureaucratic inertia -- which is why for decades the FBI continued to misinterpret vampires as being part of some wider global Communist conspiracy plot.<br /> <br /> 2. How helpful is the victim of such influence after he/she comes out from under that influence? Being possessed by a spirit and stealing files from secure storage is bad -- but if the agent in question (once the possession is over or is broken somehow) starts eagerly cooperating with the investigation and volunteers bits and pieces that he remembers that actually help uncover what's really going on, then that's going to look different.<br /> <br /> 3. What is that individual's standing or influence? If some rookie is the target of magical compulsion, it's easier to hypothesize that he's actually an enemy agent, than if it's a career agent or department head -- or somebody who's suffered some sort of personal loss to paranormals, or has some other (commonly known) emotional bias against them.<br /> <br /> As to the former point, I disagree. I think that this sort of thing fits in better with the vampires than the Garou. The werewolves' powers tend to be better suited to wrecking stuff and killing people. Even thematically, they're not well suited to subtle manipulation. Geas is a powerful gift, true. Nonetheless, it locks someone into doing something that they otherwise would not have taken the initiative to do -- but not something against their nature. As a ST, I would rule that an FBI agent turning traitor would qualify as &quot;against his instincts&quot;, and that the Geas would automatically fail as the gift is described.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T13:05:27-07:00","id":935218,"title":"","content":"The advantages that the Garou have is that they have a lot of Kinfolk (I have calculated that they have to have around one hundred Human Kinfolk and twenty-five Animal Kinfolk per existent Garou in order to support their population) and the majority of their Kinfolk are quite capable mortals who are willing to help in any way that they can. That means that there are probably a few dozen FBI agents who are secretly reporting to their Garou kin (and maybe a few Bone Gnawer or Glass Walker Animal Kinfolk who are masquerading as dogs and spying on their 'masters').","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T14:56:50-07:00","id":935281,"title":"","content":"Could a Animal kinfolk understand a concept as complicated as &quot;Spying&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T17:22:36-07:00","id":935373,"title":"","content":"It depends. Animal Kinfolk are much more intelligent than their mundane counterparts. Wolf/Dog Kinfolk could probably understand enough and could place small items in discrete places (like a potted plant). Rat Kinfolk, except for the Caged Folk, are probably not capable of doing so. Normal ravens are as intelligent as chimps, so Raven Kinfolk could probably understand anything that a human could understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T18:04:08-07:00","id":935388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/926730-pentex-and-munitions?p=935213#post935213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the latter point, it would (I think) depend on a series of considerations:<br /> <br /> 1. How receptive to the<i> idea </i>of paranormal powers is the agency (or its oversight body)? Even Twilight agencies have bureaucratic inertia -- which is why for decades the FBI continued to misinterpret vampires as being part of some wider global Communist conspiracy plot.<br /> <br /> 2. How helpful is the victim of such influence after he/she comes out from under that influence? Being possessed by a spirit and stealing files from secure storage is bad -- but if the agent in question (once the possession is over or is broken somehow) starts eagerly cooperating with the investigation and volunteers bits and pieces that he remembers that actually help uncover what's really going on, then that's going to look different.<br /> <br /> 3. What is that individual's standing or influence? If some rookie is the target of magical compulsion, it's easier to hypothesize that he's actually an enemy agent, than if it's a career agent or department head -- or somebody who's suffered some sort of personal loss to paranormals, or has some other (commonly known) emotional bias against them.<br /> <br /> As to the former point, I disagree. I think that this sort of thing fits in better with the vampires than the Garou. The werewolves' powers tend to be better suited to wrecking stuff and killing people. Even thematically, they're not well suited to subtle manipulation. Geas is a powerful gift, true. Nonetheless, it locks someone into doing something that they otherwise would not have taken the initiative to do -- but not something against their nature. As a ST, I would rule that an FBI agent turning traitor would qualify as &quot;against his instincts&quot;, and that the Geas would automatically fail as the gift is described.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The First time a case like this happens, Its kinda amusing how many protocals they'll create, putting decisions in more peoples hands, keeping someone from knowing everything. As if a supernatural whos snooping decides to take the agency on...<br /> <br /> I had to look it up, couldnt remember the name, but the Star Trek Voyager episode Cathexis is probaly could inspiration for how the SAD would react to seeing paranormals casually forcing an otherwise loyal employee to commit treason.<br /> <br /> Even the party in question might question his own fitness to return to duty. or the integrity of his memorys, after seeing what Supernaturals are capable of... how does he <i>know </i>he doesnt have anything else programmed to come into play according to some incomprehensible game.<br /> <br /> And his colleagues certainly dont know that, or that he didnt agree voluntarily, and then his memory of making the agreement was suppressed so he would THINK he was innocent.<br /> <br /> As for the Point on Geas.<br /> <br /> For a Diehard Patriot maybe, yes, but for someone who just sees being in the FBI as a job, maybe as a bit of an adventure.<br /> <br /> Aldrich Ames wasnt violating his nature.<br /> <br /> Especialy if you are also dangling a genuine Material incentive.<br /> <br /> Not sure how to sniff out if the agent your dealing with is like that though.<br /> <br /> Hmmmn any idea how the Galliard Gift Headgames would work in such a scenariao.<br /> <br /> I'd agree its a game probaly better played by vamps, but what are shadowlords but Garou trying to play the Vamps game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 07-21-2016, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T16:37:32-07:00","id":935854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/926730-pentex-and-munitions?p=935388#post935388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a Diehard Patriot maybe, yes, but for someone who just sees being in the FBI as a job, maybe as a bit of an adventure.<br /> <br /> Aldrich Ames wasnt violating his nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even in the World of Darkness, how many people join the FBI to go spy for the Soviets?<br /> <br /> Yeah, okay, if you hit Aldrich Ames with Geas -- no problemo. The <i>average</i> FBI agent, however? The average person in that sort of position will generally try to resist<i> torture </i>rather than give up state-secrets. Turning traitor just because...<br /> <br /> Yeah, I'm going to disagree with you on that one. Being an FBI agent is decidedly <i>not</i> like flipping burgers at the McDonalds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T16:55:41-07:00","id":935858,"title":"","content":"No, there is too much training involved. While they are not physically up to the level of Special Forces, the average member of the FBI is probably mentally equal to the average member of Special Forces. I would suggest that they also have the same unwillingness to betray their country because they are the best of the best. Lesser law enforcement types join state or local law enforcement agencies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T17:25:55-07:00","id":935873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/926730-pentex-and-munitions?p=935858#post935858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, there is too much training involved. While they are not physically up to the level of Special Forces, the average member of the FBI is probably mentally equal to the average member of Special Forces. I would suggest that they also have the same unwillingness to betray their country because they are the best of the best. Lesser law enforcement types join state or local law enforcement agencies.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is quite the list of dirty feds online, or just watch the movie Black Mass. They are just as fallible as any normal person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,